# Archived sources in `01_sources/` are SHA-256 hash-frozen over LF-normalised bytes and
# checked by `_tools/verify_corpus_integrity.py`, which refuses `\r\n` bytes. Without this
# rule, `core.autocrlf=true` on a Windows checkout rewrites LF blobs to CRLF in the worktree
# and breaks every archive digest on checkout.
*.md text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
